# Frontend UI/UX Engineering Standards

Apply these rules to **every** frontend change in this project (Vue, shadcn-vue, Tailwind).

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA minimum)

- Prefer semantic HTML: `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<header>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<button>`, `<label>` — avoid div-only layouts for structure.
- Meet contrast requirements for text and interactive elements; do not rely on color alone for meaning.
- Every interactive control must be keyboard reachable with a visible `:focus-visible` state.
- Images/icons that convey meaning need `alt` text or `aria-label`; decorative icons use `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Form fields: associated `<label>`, `aria-invalid` / error messages linked via `aria-describedby` where applicable.
- Live regions for async feedback (`aria-live`, toasts) when status changes matter.

## Design system & layout

- Use **design tokens** from the project theme (`style.css`, Tailwind theme, shadcn variables) — no arbitrary one-off hex/spacing unless adding a token.
- Follow an **8px spacing rhythm** (`gap-2`, `p-4`, `space-y-6`, etc.).
- Clear typography hierarchy: page title → section title → label → helper text; consistent `font-weight` and `line-height`.
- **Mobile-first** responsive layouts; test sm / md / lg breakpoints; avoid horizontal overflow on small screens.
- Reuse shadcn-vue primitives (`Button`, `Card`, `Sheet`, `Form*`) before inventing new patterns.

## Components & code quality

- Single-responsibility, reusable components; shared logic in composables (`src/composables/`).
- Always provide **loading**, **empty**, and **error** states for data-driven UI.
- Lazy-load heavy routes and charts where practical; avoid layout shift (reserve space for async content).
- Name props, events, and functions clearly; keep diffs focused — no unrelated refactors.
- Match existing project conventions (Pinia, vee-validate, `@/` imports, relation fields via `FormFieldSchema`).

## This codebase

- API calls via `src/services/`; forms via `FormBuilder` + `useFormBuilder` + Zod schemas.
- Relation fields use `type: 'relation'` and `preloadRelationFields` before edit; fetch full record on edit.
- Prefer Vite proxy in dev (`VITE_API_URL` empty); validate ZIM phone/date rules in `src/lib/validation.ts`.

## Output expectations

- Production-ready code only — no placeholder TODOs unless explicitly requested.
- Briefly note only **non-obvious** architectural or a11y decisions in the response.
